    "media:imagetext": "Sub: Agree't - City \u0026County of\nSan Francisco -\nLomita Park\nFORM 2000\nSOUTHERN PACIFIC COMPANY\n(PACIFIC LINES)\nE. R. ANTHONY.\nSUPERINTENDENT\nIN REPLY PLEASE REFER TO\nNO.\nTHIRD AND TOWNSEND STREETS\nSAN FRANCISCO, CALIF\nMarch 22nd, 1927.\nMix. Joseph J. Phillips, Right of Way Agent,\nThe City \u0026 County of San Francisco,\nRoom 375, City Hall,\nSan Francisco, California.\nDear Sir:\nReferring to your letter March 19th, 1921, making\napplication for permission to cross under Southern Pacific\nCompany's tracks and right of way near Lomita Park, Calif.,\nwith a 3-inch wrought iron water pipe, for purpose of serving\nair port to be located at that point:\nI am attaching hereto duplicate counterparts of\nproposed agreement covering. If satisfactory, kindly have\nboth copies executed by proper officers of the City and\nCounty of San Francisco, corporate seal affixed, insert date\nof execution in space provided and return original cunterpart\nto this office for filing.\nDuplicate counterpart of agreement has been fully\nexecuted on, the part of Southern Pacific Company and is to\nbe retained in your file.\nYours truly,\nSuperintendent",
